# Unity Scene Configuration: Warehouse Navigation

## Scene Overview
This scene provides a 3D visualization of a warehouse environment with a mobile robot equipped with sensors. The scene connects to ROS 2 topics to visualize sensor data and robot position in real-time.

## Robot Setup
- Robot prefab: sensor_robot.prefab
- Position: (0, 0, 0)
- Rotation: (0, 0, 0, 1)

## Environment Setup
- Ground plane: 20x20 units
- Obstacles: Shelf units, pallets, charging stations
- Lighting: Point lights at ceiling level
- Materials: Realistic textures for warehouse environment

## Sensor Visualization Components

### LiDAR Visualization
- Topic: /scan
- Component: LaserScanVisualizer.cs
- Parameters:
  - Max range: 30.0
  - Color: Green
  - Point size: 0.05

### Camera Visualization
- Topic: /camera/image_raw
- Component: CameraVisualizer.cs
- Parameters:
  - Resolution: 640x480
  - Display: On-screen texture

### IMU Visualization
- Topic: /imu
- Component: IMUVisualizer.cs
  - Orientation indicator
  - Acceleration vectors

### Odometry Visualization
- Topic: /odom
- Component: RobotPathVisualizer.cs
- Parameters:
  - Trail length: 100 points
  - Trail color: Blue

## UI Elements
- Robot status panel (battery, speed, mode)
- Sensor data display
- Navigation controls
- Waypoint markers
- Emergency stop button

## ROS Connection Settings
- IP Address: 127.0.0.1
- Port: 10000
- Message types: geometry_msgs/Twist, sensor_msgs/LaserScan, nav_msgs/Odometry

## Performance Settings
- Target frame rate: 60 FPS
- LOD bias: 1.0
- Shadow resolution: Medium
- Anti-aliasing: 2x MSAA

## Scene Behaviors
- Robot movement responds to cmd_vel topic
- Sensor data updates in real-time
- Collision detection with environment
- Path recording and visualization

## Required Assets
- Robot 3D models
- Environment textures
- UI elements
- ROS TCP connector scripts
- Visualization components

## Scene Hierarchy
- Robot (sensor_robot prefab)
  - Base
  - Wheels
  - Sensors
- Environment
  - Ground
  - Shelves
  - Obstacles
- Lighting
  - Directional light
  - Point lights
- UI
  - Canvas
  - Robot status
  - Sensor displays
- ROS Connection Manager
- Visualization Manager